      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Había una giganta llamada Nótt, la Noche, oscura como toda su familia.",
          "en": "There was a giantess named Nott, the Night, dark like all her family."
        },
        {
          "es": "Odín le dio un caballo negro, Hrímfaxi, y un carro para recorrer el cielo.",
          "en": "Odin gave her a black horse, Hrimfaxi, and a chariot to cross the sky."
        },
        {
          "es": "De la espuma de su freno cae el rocío. Por eso los valles amanecen mojados.",
          "en": "From the foam of his bit falls the dew. That is why the valleys wake up wet."
        },
        {
          "es": "Después Odín dio a su hijo, Dagr, el Día, un caballo blanco, Skinfaxi, cuya crin ilumina el mundo.",
          "en": "Then Odin gave her son, Dagr, the Day, a bright horse, Skinfaxi, whose mane lights up the world."
        },
        {
          "es": "Así, uno detrás del otro, Noche y Día recorren el cielo y dan la vuelta al mundo entero.",
          "en": "And so, one after the other, Night and Day ride across the sky and circle the whole world."
        }
