      },
      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Un día, Odín, Vili y Ve caminaban por la playa, y encontraron dos troncos arrastrados por el mar.",
          "en": "One day, Odin, Vili and Ve were walking along the shore, and found two logs washed up by the sea."
        },
        {
          "es": "Eran dos troncos sin aliento, sin mente, sin sangre ni color. Pero los dioses les dieron forma de hombre y de mujer.",
          "en": "They were two logs with no breath, no mind, no blood and no color. But the gods shaped them into a man and a woman."
        },
        {
          "es": "Odín les dio el aliento: la vida.",
          "en": "Odin gave them breath: life."
        },
        {
          "es": "Vili les dio la mente, y Ve les dio la sangre y el color de la vida.",
          "en": "Vili gave them mind, and Ve gave them blood and the color of life."
        },
        {
          "es": "Un poema antiguo, la Völuspá, nombra a los otros dos dioses Hœnir y Lodur. Pero el regalo es el mismo.",
          "en": "An old poem, the Voluspa, names the other two gods Hoenir and Lodur. But the gift is the same."
        },
        {
          "es": "Así nacieron Ask y Embla, el primer hombre y la primera mujer.",
          "en": "That is how Ask and Embla were born, the first man and the first woman."
        }
      ],
